v 3
d sshare and moransub: spatial shift-share and per-unit Moran's I
d
d sshare decomposes the growth of every unit-area pair against the
d full economy (CN = EE + ED) and, with the spatial option, against
d the neighborhood defined by a contiguity matrix (CNL = EEL + EDL).
d moransub computes Moran's I unit by unit, restricted to the
d subgraph of areas with data, with a two-tailed permutation p-value
d centered on the randomization null E[I] = -1/(n-1).
d
d Requires: Stata 16.1+
d
d Author: Jose A. Maltes
d
f sshare.ado
f sshare.sthlp
f moransub.ado
f moransub.sthlp
